Tester 1:
Liked the feature that tracks when you last hung out with a person. 
-Said that it could serve as a brutal reminder, but a useful one
-Thought that it was useful to mark in the friend profile what you did together
-Seemed slightly uncomfortable with the idea of “quantifying” relationships
AI chatbot
-Expressed that it was a cool feature
-Struggled at first to know how to use it and what it was for 
-Possible Fix: More in depth onboarding/tutorial of how to use the various features
I-message extension
-The main worry is that in order to use the app to coordinate with friends their friend also needs to have the app
-Most important functionality that the app is missing is inability to properly coordinate with people who don’t have the app
Suggestions 
-They liked the variety of suggestions, but noted that they seemed somewhat random and not necessarily suitable for the time of day/ the location of the hangout. 
-Many of the suggestions wouldn’t be chosen by the tester
Seemed to find the basic features of the app easy to use. 
-Liked the onboarding process (visually well designed) 
-Was immediately able to add contacts and then friends without help
Tab ordering/ order of operations in order to schedule a hangout
-It didn’t seem intuitive to set availability before trying to make a hangout
-Possible Fix: Consider making the availability tab the default one 
